      <div type="clause" n="23.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 23.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 23.2" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="561" ed="#liebermann"/>Nemo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="h" target="#Hn_23-2.lnote.oe.h"/> etiam de cesione<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Hn_23-2.lnote.oe.30"/> nemoris inoperati<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Hn_23-2.lnote.oe.31"/> iure cogitur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Hn_23-2.lnote.oe.32"/> respondere per witherti[h]lam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Hn_23-2.lnote.oe.33"/> nisi domino<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="i" target="#Hn_23-2.lnote.oe.i"/> suo uel captus in ea<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Hn_23-2.lnote.oe.34"/>.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 561 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_23-2.lnote.oe.h" n="h" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">wiederholt</hi> 45, 4, <hi rend="italic">wo</hi> tihla</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">repeated at 45, 4, where tihla</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_23-2.lnote.oe.i" n="i" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ausser wenn der klagende Waldbesitzer zugleich des Beklagten Herr oder Beklagter handhaft ertappt ist</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">unless the plaintiff owner of the wood is at the same time the defendant’s lord, or the defendant has been caught in the act</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_23-2.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cess. <hi rend="italic">Sc</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cess. Sc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_23-2.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">inoperti <hi rend="italic">Wi;</hi> ‘<hi rend="italic">d. i. nicht eingezäunt</hi>’ <hi rend="italic">Somner</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">inoperti Wi; ‘i.e. not fenced in’ Somner</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_23-2.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">doppelt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">twice K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_23-2.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wychterthi. <hi rend="italic">Lond;</hi> -tihtl. <hi rend="italic">Wi;</hi> -til. <hi rend="italic">Sc</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wychterthi. Lond; -tihtl. Wi; -til. Sc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_23-2.lnote.oe.34" n="34" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eo <hi rend="italic">Lond Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eo Lond Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_23-2.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">320</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Änderung zu <hi rend="italic">inoperti</hi>, einem Ggs. zu <hi rend="italic">coopertum</hi> (heutigem <hi rend="italic">covert</hi> ‘Waldesdickicht’) und die <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. II 125 als möglich angenommene Deutung ‘unumhegt’ scheint mir jetzt falsch. Ebensowenig ist an <hi rend="italic">inoperatus</hi> ‘müssig, unbeschäftigt’ (Tertullian) zu denken, das etwa einen Ggs. des Baumes zu <hi rend="italic">fructifer</hi> bilden könnte, oder an <hi rend="italic">inoperatio</hi> (Arbeitseinstellung 61, 6). Verf. meinte vielmehr: ‘Fällung von Holz (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 5), [aber] nicht [Fortnehmen von] Bearbeitetem’. <hi rend="italic">Vgl</hi>. Geffcken <hi rend="italic">Lex Salica</hi> 139</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The alteration to <hi rend="italic">inoperti</hi>, as a contrast to <hi rend="italic">coopertum</hi> (modern <hi rend="italic">covert</hi> ‘forest thicket’), and the interpretation ‘unenclosed’, accepted as possible <hi rend="italic">above</hi> II 125, now seem to me wrong. Nor should one think of <hi rend="italic">inoperatus</hi> ‘idle, unoccupied’ (Tertullian), which might perhaps form a contrast between the tree and <hi rend="italic">fructifer</hi>, or of <hi rend="italic">inoperatio</hi> (cessation of work 61, 6). Rather, the author meant: ‘the felling of wood (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 5), [but] not [the taking away of] worked material’. <hi rend="italic">Cf</hi>. Geffcken <hi rend="italic">Lex Salica</hi> 139</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_23-2.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">320</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">D. h. ‘unrechtmäßige (nicht: ‘Gegen-)klage’; <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Widerklage 2; handhaft 10. 12—<hi rend="italic">wichter thilam</hi>{33}—<hi rend="italic">eo</hi> (nämlich <hi rend="italic">nemore</hi>){34} Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">I.e. ‘unlawful (not: ‘counter-)suit’; see <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Widerklage 2; handhaft 10. 12—<hi rend="italic">wichter thilam</hi>{33}—<hi rend="italic">eo</hi> (namely <hi rend="italic">nemore</hi>){34} Rs</seg></note>
      </div>
